      "silences"
     ]
    ],
    "cites_only_retrieved": true
   },
   "answer": "Based on my search of the company's documentation, here's what I found about muting Alertmanager alerts during planned maintenance:\n\n## How to Mute Alerts in Alertmanager\n\n**Silences** are the recommended mechanism for muting alerts for a given time period [D07:5]:\n\n1. **Access the Alertmanager Web Interface** - Navigate to your Alertmanager's web UI where you can manage silences directly.\n\n2. **Create a Silence Based on Matchers** - Configure the silence using alert labels/matchers (similar to routing rules) to identify which alerts should be silenced [D07:5]. For example:\n   ```\n   {alertname=\"example\"}\n   ```\n   This would silence only alerts with the `alertname` label set to `example`.\n\n3. **Set Time Duration** - Define how long the silence should remain active.\n\n4. **In High Availability (HA) Environments** - The Alertmanager supports a \"single pane of glass\" approach where you can view/manage silences on any instance, and changes propagate across all peers [D07:4].\n\n5. **Removing/Deactivating the Silence** - To end the maintenance window silence, either delete it immediately or let it expire at its configured end time [D07:4].\n\n---\n\nNote: While the documentation explains that silences are configured in the Alertmanager web interface and covers the concept of silencing alerts, it doesn't contain specific step-by-step maintenance window procedures. For detailed operational procedures, you may want to consult the official Alertmanager vendor documentation or check the internal runbook repository for team-specific maintenance procedures.",
